~$*

# Internal docs — KEEP LOCAL ONLY. These contain IPs, server paths, infra
# details, handoff notes, and task priorities that should never land in a
# public commit. History was scrubbed in the v1.20.0 post-release pass;
# assume anything previously published remains cached on forks/clones.
CLAUDE.md
SETUP.md
.claude/
docs/HANDOFF.md
docs/TODO.md
docs/learnings.md
docs/deploy-reference.md
docs/SECURITY_ACTION_ITEMS.md
docs/https-migration.md
docs/bug140-session-analysis.md
docs/ffa-configurable-lobbies.md
docs/localization-design.md
docs/spectator-design.md
scripts/

# Dual-AI (Codex CLI) setup — LOCAL ONLY, same reason as the internal docs
# above. AGENTS.md mirrors CLAUDE.md's operational context for Codex; the
# collab scratch + dual-AI guides reference infra/workflow. The docs/ ignores
# are per-FILE (not per-dir), so each new doc is listed explicitly.
AGENTS.md
AGENTS.override.md
.codex/
ai-collab/
docs/DUAL-AI-SETUP.md
docs/CODEX-CHEATSHEET.md

# NuGet
packages/
*.nupkg

# Python caches (defensive — the backend runs in Docker, no local venv expected)
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.venv/

# Thunderstore release zip artifacts — attach to GH release, don't track in git
thunderstore/*.zip
_cm.txt

# Local analysis scratch (review-agent caches) — never publish
*.pkl
